<div class="faq">
<details><summary>When should I take it?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>Once a day, whenever it fits: before practice, after a lift, on the bus. Creatine works by building up over time, so every day beats perfect timing. Take it on rest days too.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do I still need to drink water?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>Yes. HYPR goes into 16–24 oz of water and adds the salt plain water doesn't have. Keep drinking through long, hot sessions.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will creatine make me cramp or bloat?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>Research does not show that creatine causes cramps or dehydration. Some people gain a little water weight at first. That water goes into your muscle, not your belly.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why not just drink LMNT or Liquid I.V.?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>They are hydration only. You would still need a creatine tub and a collagen tub. HYPR puts all three in one scoop, with no sugar.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is creatine a steroid?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>No. Your body makes creatine and stores it in muscle. It's also in meat and fish. HYPR uses creatine monohydrate, the most studied form.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does it taste?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><p>Watermelon, sweetened with stevia, zero sugar. Customers say it mixes smooth and isn't grainy.</p></details>
</div>
